# CODEOWNERS.example
#
# TEMPLATE — copy this to the PRIVATE config repo's root as `CODEOWNERS`
# (or `.github/CODEOWNERS` / `docs/CODEOWNERS`, per your VCS host's convention)
# and replace the placeholder handle before enabling branch-protection review.
#
# This file does NOT belong in the public vuln-reporting app repo as a live
# CODEOWNERS — it is committed here only as a reference template for the
# private config repo (Hard Rule 2 / D-02).
#
# --- Structure (D-08/D-09) ---------------------------------------------
#
# Entries are per-file, 1:1 with the deliveries.d/<team>.yaml split, so
# per-team delegation can be enabled later by swapping a single handle per
# line — no restructuring required. TODAY, every entry (including the
# default rule) resolves to the SAME placeholder: the Vulnerability
# Management team, which centrally manages and reviews all delivery files
# (D-08, central stewardship). The default `*` rule covers shared,
# cross-cutting files — contacts.yaml, the defaults: block, and the schema
# copy — so a change to the shared "who" is always a VM-team-reviewed
# change (D-09).
#
# --- Placeholder handle (D-10) ------------------------------------------
#
# `@ORG/vuln-management-team` is a PROVISIONING PLACEHOLDER. Concrete VCS
# org/team handles are filled in when the private repo is created via
# change management (long-lead; do not invent real handles here). Replace
# every occurrence below with the real team handle at repo provisioning
# time, and enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection
# (see the Plan 04 runbook).
#
# --- Reconciliation note (SC2) ------------------------------------------
#
# The roadmap's SC2 wording says a PR "requires that team's owner" as
# reviewer. This file's 1:1 per-file structure is what ENABLES that
# per-team delegation — but the roster resolves to the VM team now
# (central stewardship, D-08). That is intentional, not an unmet
# criterion: distributed per-team ownership is deferred, and can be turned
# on later by editing only the handle on the relevant line.

# Default rule — shared/cross-cutting files (contacts.yaml, defaults,
# schema copy) always reviewed by the VM team (D-09).
*                                    @ORG/vuln-management-team

# Per-team delivery files — 1:1 with deliveries.d/, one line per team file
# (D-08). All resolve to the VM team today; swap the handle per-line to
# delegate a specific team file later.
deliveries.d/exec.yaml               @ORG/vuln-management-team
deliveries.d/remediation.yaml        @ORG/vuln-management-team
deliveries.d/tag_profile.yaml        @ORG/vuln-management-team
